From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:32:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: label PPE drop reason counters

Name drop reason 122 in the debugfs reason-counter output. QSDK r42
defines it as the link-layer pause-frame sink. Naming it prevents normal
802.3x flow-control traffic from being mistaken for forwarding loss.

Label code zero as None, matching QSDK. It has no drop reason and must not
be interpreted as a business-traffic loss counter. Preserve raw counts.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -3008,6 +3008,8 @@ static const char *ppe_ft_reason_name(bo
 	}
 
 	switch (code) {
+	case 0:
+		return "None (no drop reason)";
 	case 73:
 		return "L3 no-route action drop";
 	case 74:
@@ -3018,6 +3020,8 @@ static const char *ppe_ft_reason_name(bo
 		return "L3 flow miss action drop";
 	case 80:
 		return "L2 MTU checking fail drop";
+	case 122:
+		return "pause frame";
 	default:
 		return NULL;
 	}
